  "reference_notes": "Compared the photographed triangular divided fronds on bare stipes with revised three-size pilots and all 36 variants. Replaced the generic shuttlecock outline with fewer long bare stipes and basally broad triangular fronds whose pinnae taper toward the apex. Current spring frond groups span 0.47-1.12 m and vary in upright versus spreading posture. This is expanded spring growth; tiny unfurling croziers and third-order leaflet detail are unresolved at 25 mm. Accepted as stylized bracken, pending user endorsement.",
